  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The child's golden-brown hair shimmered under the sunlight. He hugged
    a wooden sword, nearly as tall as himself, trying to lift it over his head.\r\n\n\u201CLet
    me save you, Elsa! Meine Prinzessin\u2026!\u201D\r\n\n\u201CMy princess.\" You
    gently corrected him with a smile.\r\n\nThe child mumbled something under his
    breath and continued running with his treasured sword.\r\n\n\u201CIch bin Lohengrin!!\"
    (I am Lohengrin)\r\n\n\u201COma\u2026\" He panted, \"ich mag die Geschichte nicht.
    Warum ist Lohengrin gegangen..?\u201D\r\n(Grandma, I don't like the story. why
    lohengrin left)\r\n\nYou tried to understand his words.\r\n\nFrom the balcony,
    your daughter's voice rang out:\r\n\n\u201CLeon, speak English! Oma spricht kein
    Deutsch.\u201D\r\n(Grandma doesn\u2019t speak German)\r\n\n\u201CWhy\u2026 why
    Lohengrin go from Prinzessin?\u201D\r\n\nYou gently stroked your grandson\u2019s
    head, wiping the dirt from his cheek.\r\n\n\u201CBecause we all have our own
    futures. We don\u2019t stop for each other. But that doesn\u2019t mean we don\u2019t
    love each other.\"\r\n\nLeon nodded, but you knew he didn\u2019t fully understand.\r\n\n\"Learn
    English, kiddo\u201D You smiled.\r\n\n\"I speak English, I know.\u201D\r\n\nLeon
    grumbled.\r\n\nCompared to the last time you saw him, he had grown so much.\r\n\nHe
    ran over to his father, speaking in a language you didn\u2019t understand. A
    moment later, Leon returned to your side.\r\n\n\u201COma, read story by me.\u201D\r\n\r\n\u201CLohengrin?
    Of course!\u201D\r\n\r\nYou took his hand and walked inside. It was the best
    word you could say. He skipped beside you, hugging his wooden sword tightly.\r\n\nSummer
    passed quickly, taking with it not only the heat but also the laughter.\r\n\nYou
    embraced each of your family members one by one. Leon was still clutching his
    sword, crying.\r\n\n\u201CMom, we can\u2019t let him take this on the flight\u201D\r\n\nYou
    stepped forward to soothe him.\r\n\n\"Grandma will take care of it, alright?
    Next time you come, I promise it will be just as sharp.\u201D\r\n\nYou held Leon
    close and looked at your daughter.\r\n\n\u201CWhen will you come next year?\u201D\r\n\n\u201CI\u2019m
    sorry, Mom, you know his job.\u201D\r\n\n\u201CMad, we\u2019ll try to visit more
    often.\u201D\r\n\nSummer faded quickly.\r\n\nLohengrin\u2019s wooden sword remained
    in your room.\r\n\nYour friends visited from time to time, but on some nights,
    the silence in the house felt like an invisible ocean\u2014calm yet lonely.\r\n\nIn
    the quiet, one day, you noticed a crack in the wooden sword. You searched for
    ways to mend it, making sure not to show Leon the damaged side during video calls.\r\n\nLeon
    eagerly shouted about wanting to visit America. You laughed.\r\n\r\nAnother year
    passed.\r\n\nLeon came alone this time.\r\n\nYou played with him in the backyard,
    watching as he ran and jumped, still treasuring his wooden sword.\r\n\nThen,
    at the moment he fell from the swing, you instinctively reached out to catch
    him\u2014just as you had caught every ball he\u2019d thrown before.\r\n\nYou
    twisted your back. Leon broke his arm.\r\n\nHis family arrived in America soon
    after. Their unspoken accusations weighed heavy. No words could express your
    guilt.\r\n\n\"Du solltest Leon nicht alleine mit der alten Dame lassen.\" \n(You
    shouldn\u2019t have let Leon alone with her)\r\n\n\u201CMom, I\u2019m taking
    Leon back.\u201D\r\n\n\u201CTake care of yourself, Mom. He\u2019s\u2026 busy.
    We gotta get back.\u201D\r\n\n\u2026\r\n\n\u201CI\u2019m sorry.\u201D\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6daa85973f3414a4c8d7a70af147305f, type: 2}
